      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: I'm not entirely sure what font was used for the 2018 nameplates, and as far as unicode support, I'm not entirely sure how well they were supported. But, in essence, a lot of people as of recently have been using Unicode letters to make their username look \"rare\", which can be annoying in a sense when it comes to trying to lookup users in the VRC user search and not knowing whether someone's certain letter in their username is typed or a copy paste Unicode character. I'm sure that the font itself could be updated with more support for Unicode and fonts.\n\nPersonally, I think fonts have always been a nuisance when it comes down to usernames because it makes it 10x more difficult to just lookup a user and add them. \n\nBut, on the flipside, having the ability to use username fonts does add a bit of personality to the game and more freedom to players.\n\nI personally love the old font a ton more since it was just more unique to VRChat itself and wasn't just a generic google-looking font. It was different.\n\nExample Provided:",
